#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""site-blocker - system-wide DNS blocklist for distracting sites.

Blocks porn, social media, gambling and browser-game domains through
NetworkManager's dnsmasq resolver.  Blocks whole domains *and* their
subdomains, so www./m./cdn.* are covered by a single entry.

Commands:
  site-blocker update     download fresh lists, rebuild, reload DNS
  site-blocker apply      rebuild from cached lists, reload DNS
  site-blocker pause [M]  lift blocking for M minutes (default 120, max 480)
  site-blocker resume     restore blocking immediately
  site-blocker paused     show pause state
  site-blocker heal       restore expired allow windows (boot watchdog)
  site-blocker status     show block count and test some domains
  site-blocker allow D..  allow a domain (and its subdomains)
  site-blocker block D..  block an extra domain (and its subdomains)
  site-blocker uninstall  remove everything and restore systemd-resolved
"""

